WEBVTT

00:00:00.131 --> 00:00:04.014
Chapter 5 Helena Has Two Loves.

00:00:04.074 --> 00:00:07.455
Hermia was looking for Lysander.

00:00:07.515 --> 00:00:10.727
It was very dark, and she was afraid.

00:00:10.787 --> 00:00:13.408
She called his name many times.

00:00:13.468 --> 00:00:15.480
There was no answer.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:20.722
After a few hours, she saw someone, and she began to feel happy.

00:00:20.782 --> 00:00:23.064
But it wasn't Lysander.

00:00:23.124 --> 00:00:25.226
It was Demetrius.

00:00:25.286 --> 00:00:29.039
Demetrius saw her, and he smiled.

00:00:29.099 --> 00:00:31.012
Hermia, my love.

00:00:31.072 --> 00:00:33.854
I found you, he said.

00:00:33.914 --> 00:00:35.395
Come with me.

00:00:35.455 --> 00:00:37.306
We need to go back to Athens.

00:00:37.366 --> 00:00:39.218
We need to get married.

00:00:39.278 --> 00:00:41.790
Hermia wanted to cry.

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:43.761
Where is Lysander?

00:00:43.821 --> 00:00:44.842
She asked.

00:00:44.902 --> 00:00:46.223
Lysander?

00:00:46.283 --> 00:00:47.984
Said Demetrius?

00:00:48.044 --> 00:00:49.665
I don't know.

00:00:49.725 --> 00:00:51.506
Forget about Lysander.

00:00:51.566 --> 00:00:54.729
You're going to be my wife, not his.

00:00:54.788 --> 00:00:57.540
She suddenly felt afraid.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:59.218
Demetrius?

00:00:59.277 --> 00:01:01.584
Did you hurt Lysander?

00:01:01.644 --> 00:01:02.894
She said.

00:01:02.954 --> 00:01:05.206
Did you kill him?

00:01:05.266 --> 00:01:06.656
Me?

00:01:06.716 --> 00:01:07.988
No.

00:01:08.048 --> 00:01:10.029
said Demetrius.

00:01:10.088 --> 00:01:14.140
Oberon and Puck were near Hermia and Demetrius.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:17.842
They were still laughing about poor Titania.

00:01:17.902 --> 00:01:21.384
Yes, good work Puck.

00:01:21.444 --> 00:01:23.292
said Oberon.

00:01:23.352 --> 00:01:26.479
And did you help the young lady from Athens?

00:01:26.539 --> 00:01:30.111
Did you put the juice of the flower on the man's eyes?

00:01:30.171 --> 00:01:32.102
Yes, of course.

00:01:32.161 --> 00:01:35.023
It was easy, said Puck.

00:01:35.083 --> 00:01:37.684
Oberon looked through the trees.

00:01:37.744 --> 00:01:40.195
He saw Demetrius and Hermia.

00:01:40.255 --> 00:01:42.236
That's strange.

00:01:42.296 --> 00:01:43.967
He said?

00:01:44.027 --> 00:01:48.209
There's the young man, but he's not with the right woman.

00:01:48.269 --> 00:01:51.120
They listened to Demetrius and Hermia.

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:53.203
Listen to me, Demetrius.

00:01:53.263 --> 00:01:54.726
Hermia was saying.

00:01:54.786 --> 00:01:56.577
I don't love you.

00:01:56.637 --> 00:01:58.548
I'll never love you.

00:01:58.608 --> 00:02:00.670
Don't say that, Hermia.

00:02:00.730 --> 00:02:02.311
said Demetrius.

00:02:02.371 --> 00:02:05.122
I don't want to see you ever again.

00:02:05.182 --> 00:02:06.934
said Hermia.

00:02:06.994 --> 00:02:09.416
She walked away into the wood.

00:02:09.475 --> 00:02:11.618
Demetrius watched her.

00:02:11.677 --> 00:02:13.348
I can't follow her.

00:02:13.408 --> 00:02:15.780
She's too angry, he thought.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.482
Demetrius sat down on the grass.

00:02:18.541 --> 00:02:21.356
He put his head in his hands.

00:02:21.416 --> 00:02:24.652
It's true, he thought.

00:02:24.712 --> 00:02:27.114
She doesn't love me at all.

00:02:27.174 --> 00:02:30.808
Demetrius felt very sad and very tired.

00:02:30.868 --> 00:02:33.620
In a few minutes, he was asleep.

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:36.842
Oberon was starting to feel angry.

00:02:36.902 --> 00:02:39.815
Puck, you chose the wrong man.

00:02:39.875 --> 00:02:42.728
He said, did I?

00:02:42.788 --> 00:02:44.690
said Puck.

00:02:44.749 --> 00:02:47.562
Go and find Helena.

00:02:47.622 --> 00:02:49.410
said Oberon.

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:55.590
She's a tall girl with red hair, find her, and bring her to this place.

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:57.812
Go now.

00:02:57.872 --> 00:03:00.543
Puck flew away quickly.

00:03:00.603 --> 00:03:03.094
He was afraid of Oberon.

00:03:03.154 --> 00:03:05.966
Oberon looked at Demetrius.

00:03:06.026 --> 00:03:09.798
He put the juice of the magic flower on his eyes.

00:03:09.858 --> 00:03:12.350
Now you will love Helena.

00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:13.540
He said.

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:17.141
You will only love Helena.

00:03:17.201 --> 00:03:20.472
In a few minutes, Puck came back.

00:03:20.532 --> 00:03:23.224
He was laughing.

00:03:23.284 --> 00:03:26.476
Here she is, my king.

00:03:26.535 --> 00:03:28.557
Helena is coming.

00:03:28.617 --> 00:03:30.078
He said.

00:03:30.138 --> 00:03:32.690
But she's not alone.

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:34.371
It was true.

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:36.902
Lysander was following Helena.

00:03:36.962 --> 00:03:39.694
My love, wait for me.

00:03:39.754 --> 00:03:41.255
said Lysander.

00:03:41.315 --> 00:03:43.456
I need to be near you.

00:03:43.516 --> 00:03:46.196
Helena was very angry now.

00:03:46.255 --> 00:03:49.664
For the last time, this isn't funny.

00:03:49.724 --> 00:03:52.655
Stop joking and leave me alone."

00:03:52.715 --> 00:03:54.526
She shouted.

00:03:54.586 --> 00:03:58.178
Just then Demetrius opened his eyes.

00:03:58.238 --> 00:04:00.948
He saw a very beautiful young woman.

00:04:01.008 --> 00:04:03.790
Was it a fairy or a princess?

00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:06.580
No, it was Helena.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:09.842
Did I really run away from her?

00:04:09.902 --> 00:04:11.962
Demetrius thought.

00:04:12.022 --> 00:04:13.984
I was very wrong.

00:04:14.044 --> 00:04:15.972
She's wonderful.

00:04:16.032 --> 00:04:18.090
He stood up suddenly.

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:25.452
Helena, he shouted, my love, my queen, I want to kiss you.

00:04:25.512 --> 00:04:27.892
Helena screamed.

00:04:27.952 --> 00:04:29.363
Oh no!

00:04:29.423 --> 00:04:31.903
She said, not you two.

00:04:31.923 --> 00:04:37.214
Now you're both laughing at me.

00:04:37.274 --> 00:04:40.934
She began to cry.

00:04:40.994 --> 00:04:42.954
Yes, Demetrius.

00:04:43.013 --> 00:04:44.444
said Lysander.

00:04:44.504 --> 00:04:45.875
Don't joke.

00:04:45.935 --> 00:04:48.886
Everyone knows that you love Hermia.

00:04:48.946 --> 00:04:51.828
Well, I have good news for you.

00:04:51.888 --> 00:04:53.778
She's yours.

00:04:53.838 --> 00:04:57.300
I only love Helena.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:00.071
Lysander took Helena's hand.

00:05:00.131 --> 00:05:02.583
Keep your Hermia.

00:05:02.642 --> 00:05:07.477
Said Demetrius, this is my true love.

00:05:07.537 --> 00:05:10.261
He took Helena's other hand.

00:05:10.321 --> 00:05:12.903
They both pulled on Helena's arms.

00:05:12.962 --> 00:05:14.594
Stop it!

00:05:14.654 --> 00:05:16.265
shouted Helena.

00:05:16.325 --> 00:05:20.328
At that moment, Hermia was walking somewhere near the wood.

00:05:20.388 --> 00:05:22.158
She heard voices.

00:05:22.218 --> 00:05:23.980
Is it Lysander?

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:25.190
She thought.

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:27.082
Yes, it's him.

00:05:27.141 --> 00:05:28.732
He's safe.

00:05:28.792 --> 00:05:33.876
She ran towards the voices of her friends.

00:05:33.936 --> 00:05:39.280
Chapter 6 Fighting.

00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:44.723
Hermia ran towards Lysander, and she put her arms around him.

00:05:44.783 --> 00:05:48.124
Lysander, you're safe.

00:05:48.184 --> 00:05:50.036
She said.

00:05:50.095 --> 00:05:52.526
But why did you leave me?

00:05:52.586 --> 00:05:53.987
I was all alone.

00:05:54.007 --> 00:05:57.739
I thought something terrible happened to you.

00:05:57.799 --> 00:06:00.150
Lysander's eyes were cold.

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:02.341
He turned away from her.

00:06:02.401 --> 00:06:05.052
I left because of love.

00:06:05.112 --> 00:06:06.268
He said.

00:06:06.328 --> 00:06:08.764
Hermia didn't understand.

00:06:08.823 --> 00:06:10.505
What do you mean?

00:06:10.565 --> 00:06:11.816
You love me.

00:06:11.876 --> 00:06:15.649
She said, you?

00:06:15.709 --> 00:06:18.722
Lysander laughed.

00:06:18.782 --> 00:06:22.134
No, I don't love you.

00:06:22.194 --> 00:06:25.026
I love Helena.

00:06:25.086 --> 00:06:27.208
Helena was watching them.

00:06:27.268 --> 00:06:29.980
She felt very hurt and angry.

00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:32.482
Oh, now I see.

00:06:32.542 --> 00:06:36.478
Helena said, She's part of this joke, too.

00:06:36.538 --> 00:06:39.468
Was this your idea, Hermia?

00:06:39.528 --> 00:06:41.659
What are you talking about?

00:06:41.719 --> 00:06:43.180
What joke?

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:44.821
asked Hermia.

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:46.681
You know very well.

00:06:46.741 --> 00:06:48.242
said Helena.

00:06:48.302 --> 00:06:51.192
I know Demetrius doesn't love me.

00:06:51.252 --> 00:06:53.893
Do you really think it's funny?

00:06:53.953 --> 00:06:56.194
You're my best friend.

00:06:56.254 --> 00:06:58.865
Why are you doing this to me?

00:06:58.925 --> 00:07:00.135
No, Helena.

00:07:00.195 --> 00:07:01.226
You're wrong.

00:07:01.286 --> 00:07:02.620
said Hermia.

00:07:02.680 --> 00:07:05.286
I don't know anything about a joke.

00:07:05.345 --> 00:07:07.176
Lysander, stop this.

00:07:07.236 --> 00:07:09.226
Don't laugh at Helena.

00:07:09.286 --> 00:07:10.307
Yes.

00:07:10.367 --> 00:07:12.718
Don't even talk to her Lysander.

00:07:12.778 --> 00:07:14.428
said Demetrius.

00:07:14.488 --> 00:07:16.278
I'll fight you now.

00:07:16.338 --> 00:07:17.759
Helena's mine.

00:07:17.819 --> 00:07:18.699
Yes.

00:07:18.759 --> 00:07:20.199
I'll fight you.

00:07:20.259 --> 00:07:21.750
Right now.

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:23.730
said Lysander.

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:25.821
But Hermia stopped him.

00:07:25.881 --> 00:07:27.661
She held his arms.

00:07:27.721 --> 00:07:29.932
Don't do it, Lysander.

00:07:29.992 --> 00:07:31.129
She said.

00:07:31.188 --> 00:07:32.716
He'll hurt you.

00:07:32.775 --> 00:07:35.036
Stay here with me.

00:07:35.096 --> 00:07:38.038
Lysander tried to get away from her.

00:07:38.098 --> 00:07:40.819
Demetrius laughed.

00:07:40.879 --> 00:07:44.100
Helena thought it was all part of the joke.

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:46.271
Let go of me.

00:07:46.331 --> 00:07:49.022
Lysander shouted at Hermia.

00:07:49.082 --> 00:07:50.843
Why are you here?

00:07:50.903 --> 00:07:52.734
I don't want you.

00:07:52.794 --> 00:07:56.856
Lysander, I don't understand this.

00:07:56.916 --> 00:07:58.396
said Hermia.

00:07:58.456 --> 00:08:00.447
Are you joking?

00:08:00.507 --> 00:08:03.838
Yes he is, and you're joking too.

00:08:03.898 --> 00:08:05.788
Said Helena angrily.

00:08:05.848 --> 00:08:06.979
Joking?

00:08:07.039 --> 00:08:08.370
said Lysander.

00:08:08.429 --> 00:08:09.560
No.

00:08:09.620 --> 00:08:12.931
Why can't you understand?

00:08:12.991 --> 00:08:15.642
I don't love you.

00:08:15.702 --> 00:08:18.433
I'm starting to hate you.

00:08:18.493 --> 00:08:21.834
And I love Helena.

00:08:21.894 --> 00:08:25.075
Hermia let go of Lysander.

00:08:25.135 --> 00:08:28.846
She felt sad and very surprised.

00:08:28.906 --> 00:08:30.815
It's true.

00:08:30.875 --> 00:08:32.353
She thought.

00:08:32.413 --> 00:08:34.834
He doesn't love me at all.

00:08:34.894 --> 00:08:37.514
Then she turned to Helena.

00:08:37.574 --> 00:08:39.324
You?

00:08:39.384 --> 00:08:42.065
She said in a loud angry voice.

00:08:42.125 --> 00:08:44.335
Why does he love you now?

00:08:44.395 --> 00:08:46.996
What did you do to him?

00:08:47.056 --> 00:08:49.236
I didn't do anything.

00:08:49.296 --> 00:08:50.897
said Helena.

00:08:50.956 --> 00:08:54.237
She was starting to feel afraid of her friend.

00:08:54.297 --> 00:08:57.068
You stole him from me.

00:08:57.128 --> 00:08:58.788
I'll fight you.

00:08:58.848 --> 00:09:02.191
Said Hermia, she ran towards Helena.

00:09:02.251 --> 00:09:03.692
Help!

00:09:03.752 --> 00:09:08.626
Said Helena, she hid behind Demetrius and Lysander.

00:09:08.686 --> 00:09:10.198
I know her.

00:09:10.258 --> 00:09:13.320
She's small, but she's dangerous.

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:15.031
Small?

00:09:15.092 --> 00:09:17.404
You think I'm short?

00:09:17.464 --> 00:09:18.604
said Hermia.

00:09:18.664 --> 00:09:20.286
I'm not short.

00:09:20.346 --> 00:09:22.578
You're too tall.

00:09:22.638 --> 00:09:24.059
Come here.

00:09:24.119 --> 00:09:25.480
Fight me.

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:28.902
Lysander stood between Hermia and Helena.

00:09:28.962 --> 00:09:32.293
Leave her alone, you little cat.

00:09:32.353 --> 00:09:33.944
He said to Hermia.

00:09:34.004 --> 00:09:37.036
Stay away from my beautiful Helena.

00:09:37.096 --> 00:09:39.147
She's not yours.

00:09:39.207 --> 00:09:41.168
said Demetrius.

00:09:41.228 --> 00:09:42.859
Come and fight me.

00:09:42.919 --> 00:09:44.780
Let's go over there.

00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:47.221
The prize will be beautiful Helena.

00:09:47.281 --> 00:09:48.122
Yes.

00:09:48.182 --> 00:09:49.292
Let's go.

00:09:49.352 --> 00:09:51.053
said Lysander.

00:09:51.113 --> 00:09:54.571
He turned and followed Demetrius into the wood.

00:09:54.631 --> 00:09:57.880
Hermia did not try to stop him this time.

00:09:57.940 --> 00:10:01.842
Helen and Hermia were alone together for a moment.

00:10:01.902 --> 00:10:05.276
Helena looked at Hermia's angry face.

00:10:05.336 --> 00:10:08.368
Then she quickly ran away into the wood.

00:10:08.428 --> 00:10:11.600
Now, Hermia was alone.

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:14.483
I don't understand this.

00:10:14.543 --> 00:10:15.824
She thought.

00:10:15.884 --> 00:10:18.116
What's happening to us?

00:10:18.176 --> 00:10:23.067
At the same time, Oberon and Puck were watching everything.

00:10:23.127 --> 00:10:25.996
Oberon was very angry.

00:10:26.056 --> 00:10:29.248
Did you do this, Puck?

00:10:29.308 --> 00:10:30.569
He said.

00:10:30.629 --> 00:10:33.972
I think it's funny, said Puck.

00:10:34.031 --> 00:10:37.614
Well, you must make everything right again.

00:10:37.674 --> 00:10:39.486
said Oberon.

00:10:39.546 --> 00:10:41.657
Find the two men.

00:10:41.717 --> 00:10:43.748
Keep them away from each other.

00:10:43.808 --> 00:10:45.930
They must not fight.

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:50.243
Oberon gave Puck some small green leaves.

00:10:50.303 --> 00:10:53.006
They were leaves from a magic plant.

00:10:53.066 --> 00:10:57.559
This plant could change the magic of the purple flower.

00:10:57.619 --> 00:11:05.670
When they fall asleep, put the juice of this plant on Lysander's eyes, the magic will leave him.

00:11:05.730 --> 00:11:06.950
Go.

00:11:07.010 --> 00:11:10.191
Yes, my king, said Puck.

00:11:10.251 --> 00:11:14.671
He flew away into the night.

00:11:14.732 --> 00:11:19.163
Listening activity.

00:11:19.223 --> 00:11:21.383
Ali?

00:11:21.443 --> 00:11:24.354
What are you doing here alone?

00:11:24.414 --> 00:11:27.106
Why aren't you with your friends?

00:11:27.166 --> 00:11:29.276
What friends?

00:11:29.336 --> 00:11:31.578
You have lots of friends.

00:11:31.638 --> 00:11:33.528
What about Susan?

00:11:33.589 --> 00:11:35.410
She's your best friend.

00:11:35.470 --> 00:11:37.000
She was.

00:11:37.060 --> 00:11:41.222
Now she never calls me on the phone and she never emails.

00:11:41.282 --> 00:11:44.254
Oh, well, there's still David.

00:11:44.314 --> 00:11:45.815
He's a nice boy.

00:11:45.874 --> 00:11:47.110
Or Mike.

00:11:47.170 --> 00:11:48.607
No way!

00:11:48.667 --> 00:11:52.880
David took my favourite CD and he won't give it back.

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:56.953
And when I try to do anything with Mike, he's never on time.

00:11:57.013 --> 00:12:00.055
I waited for him for two hours last time.

00:12:00.115 --> 00:12:00.936
Okay.

00:12:00.996 --> 00:12:02.547
What about Laura then?

00:12:02.607 --> 00:12:04.728
I'm not talking to her.

00:12:04.788 --> 00:12:08.031
She said bad things about me to other people.

00:12:08.091 --> 00:12:10.182
She's always doing that.

00:12:10.242 --> 00:12:11.864
There's Claire.

00:12:11.924 --> 00:12:13.516
You like Claire, don't you?

00:12:13.576 --> 00:12:14.908
No, I don't.

00:12:14.968 --> 00:12:20.289
She's so boring, always talking and talking about nothing.

00:12:20.349 --> 00:12:22.370
Who has time for that?

00:12:22.430 --> 00:12:25.500
What about the neighbor's girl, Eleanor?

00:12:25.560 --> 00:12:30.151
No, I try to be friends with her, but she doesn't like me.

00:12:30.211 --> 00:12:32.201
She doesn't like anybody.

00:12:32.261 --> 00:12:33.682
Oh.

00:12:33.742 --> 00:12:37.092
Would you like to do something with me then?

00:12:37.152 --> 00:12:43.142
Well, okay, Dad.

00:12:43.202 --> 00:12:52.973
Chapter 7 The End of the Magic Lysander ran through the wood.

00:12:53.033 --> 00:12:57.294
He was very angry, and he wanted to fight Demetrius.

00:12:57.354 --> 00:12:59.216
But where was he?

00:12:59.276 --> 00:13:03.837
He could hear Demetrius' voice, but he couldn't see him.

00:13:03.897 --> 00:13:09.590
Lysander didn't know it, but the voice was not really the voice of Demetrius.

00:13:09.650 --> 00:13:11.659
It was Puck's voice.

00:13:11.719 --> 00:13:16.042
He was using his magic to speak in Demetrius' voice.

00:13:16.102 --> 00:13:20.898
Lysander couldn't see him, but he followed him everywhere.

00:13:20.958 --> 00:13:22.569
Come on.

00:13:22.629 --> 00:13:27.174
Puck said in Demetrius' voice, fight me.

00:13:27.234 --> 00:13:29.066
Are you afraid?

00:13:29.126 --> 00:13:30.948
I'm not afraid.

00:13:31.008 --> 00:13:32.610
said Lysander.

00:13:32.670 --> 00:13:34.392
Where are you?

00:13:34.452 --> 00:13:37.363
The voice was always in front of him.

00:13:37.423 --> 00:13:39.283
He ran and ran.

00:13:39.343 --> 00:13:42.604
He followed the voice all over the wood.

00:13:42.664 --> 00:13:46.725
After several hours, Lysander was very tired.

00:13:46.785 --> 00:13:48.316
He couldn't run.

00:13:48.376 --> 00:13:50.496
He couldn't even walk.

00:13:50.556 --> 00:13:55.548
He lay down on the grass near a river and fell asleep.

00:13:55.608 --> 00:13:59.138
Then Puck did the same thing to Demetrius.

00:13:59.198 --> 00:14:04.384
He flew in front of Demetrius and spoke in Lysander's voice.

00:14:04.444 --> 00:14:10.259
Demetrius ran for hours, but of course he never found Lysander.

00:14:10.319 --> 00:14:14.471
He followed Puck to the same place where Lysander was sleeping.

00:14:14.531 --> 00:14:18.232
It was dark, and so he didn't see him.

00:14:18.292 --> 00:14:22.904
By then Demetrius was also very, very tired.

00:14:22.964 --> 00:14:29.128
He lay down on the grass and fell asleep, not far from Lysander.

00:14:29.188 --> 00:14:33.386
Next Puck looked for Helena and Hermia.

00:14:33.446 --> 00:14:41.488
They were both walking in different parts of the wood by themselves, and they were both very tired and sad.

00:14:41.548 --> 00:14:48.562
Puck used his magic, and they followed him to the place where Lysander and Demetrius were sleeping.

00:14:48.622 --> 00:14:54.806
First, Helena arrived and went to sleep, and then Hermia did the same.

00:14:54.866 --> 00:14:59.370
Puck looked at the four friends, and he laughed.

00:14:59.430 --> 00:15:04.268
Then he put the juice of the magic leaves on Lysander's eyes.

00:15:04.328 --> 00:15:07.165
The magic will leave you.

00:15:07.225 --> 00:15:08.556
said Puck.

00:15:08.616 --> 00:15:13.340
You'll think that this night was just a dream.

00:15:13.400 --> 00:15:15.862
Then Puck flew away.

00:15:15.922 --> 00:15:19.276
He wanted to tell Oberon the good news.

00:15:19.336 --> 00:15:21.557
Soon he found Oberon.

00:15:21.617 --> 00:15:25.150
Not far from the place where the four friends were sleeping.

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:27.922
Oberon had a new servant with him.

00:15:27.983 --> 00:15:30.774
It was the beautiful Indian boy.

00:15:30.834 --> 00:15:33.544
Titania gave you the boy.

00:15:33.604 --> 00:15:36.682
Puck said, you won.

00:15:36.743 --> 00:15:39.723
But Oberon did not look happy.

00:15:39.783 --> 00:15:43.894
Yes, she gave me the boy very easily.

00:15:43.954 --> 00:15:46.804
She forgot that we were arguing.

00:15:46.864 --> 00:15:48.845
She forgot about me.

00:15:48.905 --> 00:15:52.546
She can only think about that monster.

00:15:52.606 --> 00:15:55.566
He pointed at Titania and Bottom.

00:15:55.626 --> 00:15:58.727
They were sitting under a large tree.

00:15:58.787 --> 00:16:04.446
Titania was looking at Bottom's horrible face and smiling.

00:16:04.506 --> 00:16:07.266
What do you want, my dear?"

00:16:07.326 --> 00:16:09.608
She said in her soft voice.

00:16:09.668 --> 00:16:11.050
Some music?

00:16:11.110 --> 00:16:12.500
Flowers?

00:16:12.560 --> 00:16:15.362
Titania's fairy servants came.

00:16:15.422 --> 00:16:19.056
They sang and played beautiful music for Bottom.

00:16:19.116 --> 00:16:25.310
Some fairies brought flowers, and Titania put them around Bottom's big ears.

00:16:25.370 --> 00:16:28.202
And what would you like to eat?

00:16:28.262 --> 00:16:30.044
asked Titania.

00:16:30.104 --> 00:16:34.948
Or I'd like some grass please.

00:16:35.007 --> 00:16:38.660
Some nice tall grass.

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:42.532
Or I could eat these flowers.

00:16:42.592 --> 00:16:46.676
Said Bottom in his strange donkey's voice.

00:16:46.736 --> 00:16:48.247
Anything.

00:16:48.307 --> 00:16:49.918
said Titania.

00:16:49.978 --> 00:16:52.924
She looked at Bottom and smiled.

00:16:52.984 --> 00:16:55.308
You're so beautiful.

00:16:55.368 --> 00:16:56.759
Your eyes.

00:16:56.819 --> 00:16:58.120
Your voice.

00:16:58.180 --> 00:17:00.801
Your wonderful ears.

00:17:00.861 --> 00:17:03.373
I love you so much."

00:17:03.432 --> 00:17:07.054
Bottom ate a good meal of grass and flowers.

00:17:07.115 --> 00:17:10.816
And then he and Titania fell asleep under the tree.

00:17:10.877 --> 00:17:13.807
The fairies sang to them.

00:17:13.868 --> 00:17:17.680
Oberon looked at Titania and Bottom.

00:17:17.739 --> 00:17:20.191
I thought it was funny at first.

00:17:20.251 --> 00:17:21.782
He said to Puck.

00:17:21.842 --> 00:17:23.752
But now I'm sorry.

00:17:23.812 --> 00:17:26.283
It's time to stop the magic.

00:17:26.343 --> 00:17:32.665
He put the magic leaves on Titania's eyes, and the magic of the flower left her.

00:17:32.725 --> 00:17:35.035
Wake up, my queen.

00:17:35.095 --> 00:17:37.556
Oberon said softly.

00:17:37.616 --> 00:17:40.787
Titania woke up and smiled.

00:17:40.847 --> 00:17:45.948
Oberon, I had such a strange dream.

00:17:46.008 --> 00:17:49.493
In my dream, I loved a monster.

00:17:49.553 --> 00:17:50.748
She said.

00:17:50.808 --> 00:17:54.150
Then she saw Bottom and she screamed.

00:17:54.211 --> 00:17:55.381
Oh!

00:17:55.441 --> 00:17:57.592
He's horrible!

00:17:57.652 --> 00:18:00.544
She jumped up and hit her face.

00:18:00.605 --> 00:18:03.216
Oberon put his arms around her.

00:18:03.277 --> 00:18:06.548
The bad dreams are over, my love.

00:18:06.608 --> 00:18:08.420
He said.

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:12.413
It's almost time for Theseus and Hippolyta's wedding.

00:18:12.473 --> 00:18:14.354
We must go to Athens.

00:18:14.414 --> 00:18:18.972
We'll bring good luck to Theseus and Hippolyta at their wedding tomorrow.

00:18:19.032 --> 00:18:22.679
Oberon called Puck and spoke to him.

00:18:22.739 --> 00:18:27.592
Puck used his magic and he took the donkey's head away from Bottom.

00:18:27.652 --> 00:18:32.416
Then Oberon and Titania walked through the wood together.

00:18:32.476 --> 00:18:40.289
Titania saw Lysander, Demetrius, Helena and Hermia on the grass and she laughed.

00:18:40.350 --> 00:18:42.569
Who are they?

00:18:42.630 --> 00:18:43.670
She asked.

00:18:43.730 --> 00:18:48.542
They are four friends who had a very bad night, and they need to sleep.

00:18:48.602 --> 00:18:50.364
said Oberon.

00:18:50.424 --> 00:18:52.955
Titania called her servants.

00:18:53.015 --> 00:18:55.686
Sing to them fairies.

00:18:55.746 --> 00:18:57.057
She said.

00:18:57.117 --> 00:19:00.269
They must sleep until the morning.

00:19:00.329 --> 00:19:08.265
The fairies sang and played music, and the four friends slept all night.

00:19:08.325 --> 00:19:12.800
Listening activity.

00:19:12.860 --> 00:19:14.600
Hello.

00:19:14.661 --> 00:19:16.302
Seaside Dinner Theatre.

00:19:16.362 --> 00:19:17.562
Can I help you?

00:19:17.622 --> 00:19:18.814
Yes.

00:19:18.874 --> 00:19:22.196
I want to see the play tonight and have dinner.

00:19:22.256 --> 00:19:23.336
Good.

00:19:23.396 --> 00:19:25.538
Can I have your name, please?

00:19:25.598 --> 00:19:28.410
My last name is Farrell.

00:19:28.470 --> 00:19:36.374
That's F-A-R-R-E-L-L.

00:19:36.434 --> 00:19:38.336
Thank you, Miss Farrell.

00:19:38.396 --> 00:19:40.231
How many people are going?

00:19:40.292 --> 00:19:42.186
And there will be four of us.

00:19:42.246 --> 00:19:43.366
OK.

00:19:43.426 --> 00:19:45.697
The play starts at eight o'clock.

00:19:45.757 --> 00:19:46.887
Good.

00:19:46.947 --> 00:19:48.798
What's the play again?

00:19:48.858 --> 00:19:49.648
I forget.

00:19:49.668 --> 00:19:52.158
A midsummer night's dream.

00:19:52.218 --> 00:19:53.528
It's a great show.

00:19:53.588 --> 00:19:54.889
You'll love it.

00:19:54.949 --> 00:19:57.769
But that's a very long play.

00:19:57.829 --> 00:20:00.190
Isn't it three or four hours?

00:20:00.250 --> 00:20:03.350
Oh, we're not showing the whole play.

00:20:03.410 --> 00:20:05.140
Just the best parts.

00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:07.584
The show will be over at ten o'clock.

00:20:07.644 --> 00:20:08.816
Okay.

00:20:08.876 --> 00:20:12.098
Now, how much is that going to be?

00:20:12.158 --> 00:20:14.320
That will be £120.

00:20:14.380 --> 00:20:17.262
You can pay at the door.

00:20:17.322 --> 00:20:18.083
Really?

00:20:18.103 --> 00:20:21.535
I didn't think it was so expensive.

00:20:21.595 --> 00:20:23.376
Oh, sorry.

00:20:23.436 --> 00:20:25.558
That's all the tickets together.

00:20:25.618 --> 00:20:28.489
It's £30 for each ticket.

00:20:28.549 --> 00:20:31.852
And the ticket is for the play and dinner.

00:20:31.912 --> 00:20:33.692
That's much better.

00:20:33.752 --> 00:20:34.623
Okay.

00:20:34.683 --> 00:20:36.099
Thank you very much.

00:20:36.159 --> 00:20:37.404
Thank you.

00:20:37.464 --> 00:20:40.756
Enjoy the show.

00:20:40.817 --> 00:20:51.773
Acting in theatres in Shakespeare's time Four hundred years ago during Shakespeare's life theatres and acting were very different.

00:20:51.833 --> 00:20:54.094
First there were no actresses.

00:20:54.154 --> 00:21:00.237
Boys acted as the young women in Shakespeare's plays and old men acted as the old women.

00:21:00.297 --> 00:21:08.248
This is why in a Midsummer Night's Dream, Bottom and the other actors are all men, but one of them will be a lady in their play.

00:21:08.308 --> 00:21:13.898
The first people who acted as Hermia, Helena and Titania were boys.

00:21:13.958 --> 00:21:21.580
Sometimes actors performed plays at the homes of people who were very rich or important, like the Queen.

00:21:21.640 --> 00:21:27.592
At the end of a Midsummer Night's Dream, Duke Theseus watches a play at his home.

00:21:27.652 --> 00:21:30.574
theatres were also very different.

00:21:30.634 --> 00:21:32.598
The theatres were large.

00:21:32.658 --> 00:21:36.769
Almost 3,000 people could see a play at the same time.

00:21:36.829 --> 00:21:41.750
If these people didn't like the play, they usually made a lot of noise.

00:21:41.810 --> 00:21:45.322
The theatres also usually had no roofs.

00:21:45.382 --> 00:21:49.262
When it rained, the people who watched the plays got wet.

00:21:49.322 --> 00:21:52.844
And this was in England, where it often rains.

00:21:52.904 --> 00:21:56.455
Many people had to stand up for the whole play.

00:21:56.515 --> 00:21:59.986
People who paid more for a ticket could sit down.

00:22:00.046 --> 00:22:02.968
All of the plays started in the afternoon.

00:22:03.028 --> 00:22:05.408
There were no special lights.

00:22:05.468 --> 00:22:15.182
Most of the story in a Midsummer Night's Dream happens at night, but the actors of Shakespeare's times probably performed in the afternoon sun.

00:22:15.242 --> 00:22:21.364
Shakespeare's favourite theatre was the Globe, which burned down in 1613.

00:22:21.424 --> 00:22:26.312
In 1996 some people in London built a copy of this theatre.

00:22:26.372 --> 00:22:33.142
They built this copy at the same place where the old globe stood and it is just like the old theatre.

00:22:33.202 --> 00:22:38.225
Go and see a play there when you are in London.

00:22:38.285 --> 00:22:49.272
Chapter 8 Three Weddings Hermia, Helena, Lysander and Demetrius continued to sleep.

00:22:49.332 --> 00:22:52.544
The morning came and then it was noon.

00:22:52.604 --> 00:22:54.522
The wood was quiet.

00:22:54.582 --> 00:22:58.671
and suddenly there was the noise of horses and people.

00:22:58.731 --> 00:23:03.884
It was Theseus and Hippolyta with their servants and some of their friends.

00:23:03.944 --> 00:23:07.665
Egeus, Hermia's father, was with them.

00:23:07.726 --> 00:23:09.706
They were hunting in the wood.

00:23:09.767 --> 00:23:13.988
They all stopped when they saw the four young people on the grass.

00:23:14.048 --> 00:23:16.720
That's my daughter!

00:23:16.780 --> 00:23:18.030
said Egeus.

00:23:18.090 --> 00:23:20.392
What is she doing here?

00:23:20.452 --> 00:23:23.557
And Lysander, and Demetrius.

00:23:23.617 --> 00:23:29.175
Wake them, said Theseus, and his servants blew their horns.

00:23:29.236 --> 00:23:32.688
The four young people woke up and looked around.

00:23:32.748 --> 00:23:35.280
They were very surprised.

00:23:35.340 --> 00:23:38.213
What are you all doing here?

00:23:38.273 --> 00:23:39.904
said Theseus.

00:23:39.964 --> 00:23:42.276
Lysander stood up.

00:23:42.336 --> 00:23:44.398
I came here with Hermia.

00:23:44.458 --> 00:23:46.660
We wanted to run away together.

00:23:46.720 --> 00:23:49.152
I love her very much.

00:23:49.212 --> 00:23:51.074
And I want to marry her.

00:23:51.134 --> 00:23:52.470
He said.

00:23:52.530 --> 00:23:54.596
Hermia smiled.

00:23:54.656 --> 00:23:57.126
So he doesn't love Helena?

00:23:57.186 --> 00:23:58.447
She thought.

00:23:58.507 --> 00:24:01.048
It was all a dream.

00:24:01.108 --> 00:24:03.788
But Egeus was very angry.

00:24:03.848 --> 00:24:06.100
Never, he said.

00:24:06.160 --> 00:24:09.760
Hermia, you're going to marry Demetrius.

00:24:09.820 --> 00:24:12.662
Isn't that right, Demetrius?

00:24:12.722 --> 00:24:15.362
Demetrius stood up.

00:24:15.423 --> 00:24:19.654
He spoke to Egeus, but he looked only at Helena.

00:24:19.714 --> 00:24:22.882
I'm sorry, sir, but it's not true.

00:24:22.942 --> 00:24:26.742
I did love Hermia, but that love is gone.

00:24:26.802 --> 00:24:31.156
Now I love Helena, and I will always love her.

00:24:31.216 --> 00:24:36.218
Finally, Helena understood that Demetrius was not joking.

00:24:36.279 --> 00:24:38.880
She wanted to cry with happiness.

00:24:38.941 --> 00:24:41.622
She put her arms around Demetrius.

00:24:41.682 --> 00:24:44.864
Well, said Theseus.

00:24:44.924 --> 00:24:49.248
Then there will be three weddings today and not just one.

00:24:49.308 --> 00:24:53.364
Come back to Athens and we will all celebrate together.

00:24:53.423 --> 00:24:56.228
They all went back to the city.

00:24:56.288 --> 00:25:01.189
On the way, the four friends talked about their strange dream.

00:25:01.249 --> 00:25:05.460
At the same time, Bottom was still asleep under the tree.

00:25:05.520 --> 00:25:08.691
He woke up suddenly and looked around.

00:25:08.751 --> 00:25:10.832
What a dream!

00:25:10.892 --> 00:25:12.072
He thought.

00:25:12.132 --> 00:25:15.793
Strange and wonderful.

00:25:15.853 --> 00:25:20.324
He remembered the donkey's head and the beautiful fairy queen.

00:25:20.384 --> 00:25:23.670
I'll tell Peter Quince about my dream.

00:25:23.730 --> 00:25:26.106
He can write a song about it.

00:25:26.166 --> 00:25:28.827
I can sing it for Theseus.

00:25:28.887 --> 00:25:31.408
Then he remembered the wedding.

00:25:31.468 --> 00:25:33.239
Theseus is wedding.

00:25:33.299 --> 00:25:34.169
He shouted.

00:25:34.229 --> 00:25:35.410
The play.

00:25:35.470 --> 00:25:37.430
I have to find my friends.

00:25:37.490 --> 00:25:40.282
Bottom ran towards the city.

00:25:40.342 --> 00:25:44.773
The three weddings were full of music and dancing and flowers.

00:25:44.833 --> 00:25:46.994
Even Egeus was happy.

00:25:47.054 --> 00:25:51.878
After the weddings, there was another party at Theseus's beautiful house.

00:25:51.938 --> 00:25:55.022
Theseus decided to watch the play.

00:25:55.082 --> 00:25:58.345
Bottom friends were at Peter Quince's house.

00:25:58.405 --> 00:26:03.398
They were trying to practice, but the play needed a hero.

00:26:03.458 --> 00:26:06.020
And someone came to the door.

00:26:06.080 --> 00:26:10.294
It was Theseus's servant, and he had a letter for them.

00:26:10.354 --> 00:26:13.106
Peter Quince read the letter.

00:26:13.166 --> 00:26:16.218
Then he sat down with his head in his hands.

00:26:16.278 --> 00:26:20.245
This is terrible news, he said.

00:26:20.305 --> 00:26:25.481
The Duke wants to see our play, but we can't do the play without Bottom!

00:26:25.542 --> 00:26:27.362
Who'll be our hero?

00:26:27.382 --> 00:26:29.052
I will!

00:26:29.112 --> 00:26:30.983
Said a voice at the door.

00:26:31.043 --> 00:26:33.004
They all turned to look.

00:26:33.064 --> 00:26:34.584
It was Bottom.

00:26:34.644 --> 00:26:36.325
Bottom!

00:26:36.385 --> 00:26:38.175
You're safe!

00:26:38.236 --> 00:26:40.606
You're not a monster!

00:26:40.666 --> 00:26:44.888
His friend said, and they all put their arms around him.

00:26:44.948 --> 00:26:46.946
Bottom smiled.

00:26:47.006 --> 00:26:50.998
Does Theseus really want to see our play?"

00:26:51.058 --> 00:26:52.299
He said.

00:26:52.360 --> 00:26:54.672
Then we don't have much time.

00:26:54.732 --> 00:26:56.484
Let's get ready!

00:26:56.544 --> 00:27:04.192
Theseus, Hippolyta, Lysander, Hermia, Helena and Demetrius all watched the play together.

00:27:04.252 --> 00:27:11.461
Bottom and his friends made a lot of mistakes, and sometimes Lysander or Demetrius laughed.

00:27:11.521 --> 00:27:14.086
but the actors tried very hard.

00:27:14.146 --> 00:27:18.298
Afterwards, Theseus gave them a large bag of gold.

00:27:18.358 --> 00:27:22.982
They were all very happy, but the happiest was Bottom.

00:27:23.042 --> 00:27:25.784
Soon it was time to go to bed.

00:27:25.844 --> 00:27:28.356
The moon was high in the sky.

00:27:28.416 --> 00:27:30.638
Everyone fell asleep.

00:27:30.698 --> 00:27:35.904
Then Titania, Oberon, Puck, and all the fairies arrived.

00:27:35.964 --> 00:27:38.788
They danced through all the rooms of the house.

00:27:38.848 --> 00:27:40.799
They danced until morning.

00:27:40.859 --> 00:27:47.422
They brought good luck to the house and good luck to everyone who slept there.

00:27:47.482 --> 00:28:23.296
A Midsummer Night's Dream by William Shakespeare Copyright Black Cat Publishing William Shakespeare Most people think that William Shakespeare is the greatest writer in the English language, but we don't know much about his life.

00:28:23.356 --> 00:28:32.089
He was born in the town of Stratford-upon-Avon in Central England, probably on the 23rd of April 1564.

00:28:32.149 --> 00:28:37.831
His father was a glovemaker, and his mother was the daughter of a rich farmer.

00:28:37.891 --> 00:28:41.191
William had seven brothers and sisters.

00:28:41.251 --> 00:28:47.635
He went to school and studied Greek and Latin and the works of many famous poets.

00:28:47.695 --> 00:28:53.790
When he was 18, he married Anne Hathaway, who was eight years older than him.

00:28:53.850 --> 00:28:55.802
They had three children.

00:28:55.862 --> 00:29:04.162
Susanna was born in 1582, and Hamnet and Judith, who were twins, were born in 1585.

00:29:04.222 --> 00:29:12.139
William went to live in London a few years later, but Anne and the children stayed in Stratford-upon-Avon.

00:29:12.199 --> 00:29:17.751
In London, Shakespeare became an actor, and later he became a writer.

00:29:17.812 --> 00:29:24.655
He wrote 40 plays and many poems between 1592 and 1613.

00:29:24.715 --> 00:29:31.674
Some of his most famous plays were Hamlet, Romeo and Juliet and King Lear.

00:29:31.734 --> 00:29:37.032
He wrote a Midsummer Night's Dream in 1595.

00:29:37.092 --> 00:29:41.504
Shakespeare's plays were popular and he became rich.

00:29:41.564 --> 00:29:45.536
He bought a good house in Stratford-upon-Avon for his family.

00:29:45.596 --> 00:29:48.507
But there were sad times as well.

00:29:48.567 --> 00:29:55.189
His son, Hamnet, died in 1596 when he was only 11 years old.

00:29:55.249 --> 00:30:01.330
Some people also think that Shakespeare and Anne Hathaway were not happy together.

00:30:01.390 --> 00:30:07.142
Near the end of his life, Shakespeare moved back to his home in Stratford-upon-Avon.

00:30:07.202 --> 00:30:13.434
He died there on 23 April 1616, on his birthday.

00:30:13.494 --> 00:30:18.886
Now people read and study Shakespeare's plays and poems everywhere.

00:30:18.946 --> 00:30:29.040
People still perform his plays all over the world, and there are also hundreds of films of Shakespeare's plays.

00:30:29.100 --> 00:30:33.384
Listening activity.

00:30:33.444 --> 00:30:35.706
Example.

00:30:35.766 --> 00:30:38.648
Titania.

00:30:38.708 --> 00:30:41.150
One.

00:30:41.210 --> 00:30:44.173
Lysander.

00:30:44.233 --> 00:30:46.494
Two.

00:30:46.554 --> 00:30:49.687
Demetrius.

00:30:49.747 --> 00:30:52.329
Three.

00:30:52.390 --> 00:30:54.972
Hermia.

00:30:55.032 --> 00:30:57.264
Four.

00:30:57.324 --> 00:30:59.850
Theseus.

00:30:59.910 --> 00:31:02.316
5.

00:31:02.376 --> 00:31:18.743
Hippolyta Chapter 1 Trouble in Athens Everyone in the city of Athens was getting ready for a wonderful celebration.

00:31:18.803 --> 00:31:24.806
In a few days, their duke, Theseus, was going to marry the beautiful Hippolyta.

00:31:24.866 --> 00:31:35.268
Theseus and Hippolyta walked through the city streets together, hand in hand. “Four days,” said Theseus.

00:31:35.328 --> 00:31:37.129
"It's a long time.

00:31:37.189 --> 00:31:39.050
I want to marry you now."

00:31:39.110 --> 00:31:41.802
Hippolyta smiled at him.

00:31:41.862 --> 00:31:46.304
Just then they saw Theseus's friend, Egeus.

00:31:46.364 --> 00:31:50.756
He was walking quickly towards them, and he looked very angry.

00:31:50.816 --> 00:31:54.457
He was holding his daughter, Hermia, by her arm.

00:31:54.517 --> 00:31:56.606
She didn't want to go with him.

00:31:56.666 --> 00:32:00.025
Hermia was quite short with blonde hair.

00:32:00.085 --> 00:32:05.786
She was small and very pretty, but she was a strong person inside.

00:32:05.846 --> 00:32:09.537
Two young men followed Hermia and her father.

00:32:09.597 --> 00:32:15.088
They were Lysander and Demetrius, and they both loved Hermia.

00:32:15.148 --> 00:32:20.632
Lysander didn't have much money, but he was very handsome and kind.

00:32:20.692 --> 00:32:29.297
Demetrius was also handsome, and he was rich, but sometimes he was unkind, and he often got angry easily.

00:32:29.357 --> 00:32:32.848
Duke Theseus, you must help me.

00:32:32.908 --> 00:32:34.018
said Egeus.

00:32:34.078 --> 00:32:36.719
It's my daughter, Hermia.

00:32:36.779 --> 00:32:40.330
I chose this man, Demetrius, for her.

00:32:40.390 --> 00:32:44.131
He wants to marry her, but she won't do it.

00:32:44.191 --> 00:32:45.621
Why Hermia?

00:32:45.681 --> 00:32:47.142
Ask Theseus.

00:32:47.202 --> 00:32:49.255
Demetrius is a good man.

00:32:49.315 --> 00:32:52.350
Lysander is a good man too.

00:32:52.410 --> 00:32:54.042
said Hermia.

00:32:54.102 --> 00:32:55.603
And I love him.

00:32:55.623 --> 00:33:00.096
I don't love Demetrius and I will never marry him.

00:33:00.156 --> 00:33:01.237
I agree.

00:33:01.297 --> 00:33:02.998
said Lysander.

00:33:03.058 --> 00:33:05.850
Hermia's father likes Demetrius.

00:33:05.910 --> 00:33:07.232
That's fine.

00:33:07.292 --> 00:33:09.042
He can marry him.

00:33:09.102 --> 00:33:10.664
I'll take Hermia.

00:33:10.724 --> 00:33:12.205
I'll fight you for that.

00:33:12.265 --> 00:33:13.686
said Demetrius.

00:33:13.746 --> 00:33:17.239
Demetrius, you're forgetting about Helena.

00:33:17.299 --> 00:33:18.824
said Hermia.

00:33:18.884 --> 00:33:22.128
Helena was Hermia's best friend.

00:33:22.188 --> 00:33:26.399
A few months before Helena and Demetrius were in love.

00:33:26.459 --> 00:33:30.330
Then Demetrius suddenly fell in love with Hermia instead.

00:33:30.390 --> 00:33:33.252
Now Demetrius never talked to Helena.

00:33:33.312 --> 00:33:36.172
Helena still loves you very much.

00:33:36.232 --> 00:33:37.383
said Hermia.

00:33:37.443 --> 00:33:39.473
You broke her heart.

00:33:39.534 --> 00:33:41.354
That was a long time ago.

00:33:41.414 --> 00:33:42.804
said Demetrius.

00:33:42.865 --> 00:33:44.559
It was a mistake.

00:33:44.619 --> 00:33:46.964
You're going to marry me, Hermia.

00:33:47.024 --> 00:33:49.846
Your father wants it, and I want it.

00:33:49.906 --> 00:33:52.407
Egeus turned to Theseus.

00:33:52.467 --> 00:33:55.639
Duke, please help me.

00:33:55.699 --> 00:33:57.240
I'm sorry, Hermia.

00:33:57.300 --> 00:33:59.291
You must listen to your father.

00:33:59.351 --> 00:34:00.932
said Theseus.

00:34:00.992 --> 00:34:06.304
Later, Hermia and Lysander were alone together on a quiet street.

00:34:06.365 --> 00:34:08.846
Hermia felt afraid and sad.

00:34:08.906 --> 00:34:11.209
She began to cry.

00:34:11.269 --> 00:34:15.302
Lysander, I can't marry that man.

00:34:15.363 --> 00:34:17.744
I want to be with you.

00:34:17.804 --> 00:34:20.816
Lysander put his arms around her.

00:34:20.876 --> 00:34:22.427
He had a plan.

00:34:22.488 --> 00:34:24.619
We can run away together.

00:34:24.679 --> 00:34:26.170
He told Hermia.

00:34:26.231 --> 00:34:28.872
I have an aunt who lives far away.

00:34:28.933 --> 00:34:30.364
We can go there.

00:34:30.423 --> 00:34:32.194
We'll be safe with her.

00:34:32.254 --> 00:34:34.577
Then I can marry you.

00:34:34.636 --> 00:34:36.498
Meet me tomorrow night.

00:34:36.558 --> 00:34:39.840
We'll leave the city and we'll never come back.

00:34:39.901 --> 00:34:42.035
Of course I'll be there.

00:34:42.095 --> 00:34:43.308
said Hermia.

00:34:43.368 --> 00:34:45.639
I'll go anywhere with you.

00:34:45.699 --> 00:34:48.270
Just then, they saw Helena.

00:34:48.330 --> 00:34:51.941
Helena was a tall, pretty girl with red hair.

00:34:52.001 --> 00:34:56.922
She often looked sad because she thought about Demetrius day and night.

00:34:56.982 --> 00:34:59.533
You're so lucky, Hermia.

00:34:59.593 --> 00:35:00.933
Helena said.

00:35:00.993 --> 00:35:05.554
Demetrius loves you, and he doesn't even want to look at me.

00:35:05.614 --> 00:35:08.166
And now he's going to marry you.

00:35:08.226 --> 00:35:11.170
Don't worry, said Lysander.

00:35:11.230 --> 00:35:13.711
That will never happen.

00:35:13.771 --> 00:35:16.582
They told Helena about their plan.

00:35:16.642 --> 00:35:18.524
I'll miss you, Helena.

00:35:18.584 --> 00:35:19.864
Hermia said.

00:35:19.924 --> 00:35:21.446
But think of it.

00:35:21.506 --> 00:35:23.086
I'll be far away.

00:35:23.147 --> 00:35:25.328
Demetrius will forget about me.

00:35:25.388 --> 00:35:27.169
He'll love you again.

00:35:27.229 --> 00:35:29.890
But Helena was not so sure.

00:35:29.950 --> 00:35:33.682
Hermia and Lysander walked away hand in hand.

00:35:33.742 --> 00:35:37.616
They were smiling and talking about their new life together.

00:35:37.676 --> 00:35:40.558
Helena sat alone and watched them.

00:35:40.618 --> 00:35:43.609
She thought about Demetrius for a long time.

00:35:43.669 --> 00:35:46.350
Then she had an idea.

00:35:46.410 --> 00:35:50.181
I'll tell Demetrius about Hermia's plan.

00:35:50.241 --> 00:35:52.992
He'll go to her, but he'll thank me.

00:35:53.052 --> 00:35:54.523
He'll talk to me.

00:35:54.583 --> 00:35:56.474
He'll smile at me.

00:35:56.534 --> 00:35:58.244
I'll tell him now.

00:35:58.304 --> 00:36:02.886
Helena ran to Demetrius's house.

00:36:02.946 --> 00:36:07.308
Listening activity.

00:36:07.368 --> 00:36:09.800
Example.

00:36:09.860 --> 00:36:14.203
I told Hermia to listen to her father.

00:36:14.263 --> 00:36:16.494
One.

00:36:16.554 --> 00:36:20.356
I will never marry Demetrius.

00:36:20.417 --> 00:36:22.518
Two.

00:36:22.578 --> 00:36:26.540
Hermia and I will run away together.

00:36:26.600 --> 00:36:28.732
Three.

00:36:28.792 --> 00:36:33.725
I'll tell Demetrius about Hermia and Lysander's plan.

00:36:33.785 --> 00:36:35.636
Four.

00:36:35.696 --> 00:36:39.598
I chose Demetrius for my daughter.

00:36:39.658 --> 00:36:41.710
5.

00:36:41.770 --> 00:36:44.141
Hermia has to marry me.

00:36:44.201 --> 00:36:49.044
I want it, and her father wants it too.

00:36:49.104 --> 00:36:52.588
Chapter 2.

00:36:52.648 --> 00:37:01.404
Trouble in the Wood In the Wood, two other people were unhappy because of love, but they weren't real people.

00:37:01.464 --> 00:37:04.224
They were the king and queen of the fairies.

00:37:04.284 --> 00:37:08.362
beautiful Titania and dark handsome Oberon.

00:37:08.422 --> 00:37:13.224
They loved each other very much, but today they were arguing.

00:37:13.284 --> 00:37:17.656
Titania had a new servant, a beautiful Indian boy.

00:37:17.716 --> 00:37:22.428
Oberon needed a servant and he wanted the Indian boy for himself.

00:37:22.489 --> 00:37:24.779
Titania did not agree.

00:37:24.840 --> 00:37:28.421
In the evening they saw each other in the wood.

00:37:28.481 --> 00:37:31.032
Titania was walking with her fairies.

00:37:31.092 --> 00:37:33.848
They were dancing all around her.

00:37:33.908 --> 00:37:36.214
My Queen.

00:37:36.274 --> 00:37:38.266
said Oberon.

00:37:38.326 --> 00:37:41.719
Titania saw Oberon and turned away.

00:37:41.780 --> 00:37:44.312
I won't speak to you.

00:37:44.372 --> 00:37:45.933
She said.

00:37:45.994 --> 00:37:48.346
Why are we fighting?

00:37:48.406 --> 00:37:50.187
Just give me the boy.

00:37:50.247 --> 00:37:51.748
said Oberon.

00:37:51.808 --> 00:37:54.401
I will never give him to you.

00:37:54.461 --> 00:37:55.532
Goodbye.

00:37:55.592 --> 00:37:57.083
said Titania.

00:37:57.144 --> 00:37:59.962
The Queen and her fairies walked away.

00:38:00.022 --> 00:38:02.462
Oberon felt very angry.

00:38:02.522 --> 00:38:05.024
Why won't she give me the boy?

00:38:05.084 --> 00:38:06.866
He said to himself.

00:38:06.926 --> 00:38:10.088
Why is she so cold to me?

00:38:10.148 --> 00:38:12.340
She'll be sorry for this.

00:38:12.400 --> 00:38:15.712
Then he remembered a special place in the wood.

00:38:15.772 --> 00:38:18.655
A small purple flower grew there.

00:38:18.715 --> 00:38:21.058
This flower was magic.

00:38:21.118 --> 00:38:23.730
Oberon had an idea.

00:38:23.790 --> 00:38:26.232
He called his servant Puck.

00:38:26.292 --> 00:38:28.402
Puck was a goblin.

00:38:28.462 --> 00:38:33.124
He was a very mischievous goblin and loved making trouble.

00:38:33.184 --> 00:38:36.446
Oberon told Puck about the flower.

00:38:36.506 --> 00:38:43.600
If you put the juice of this flower on someone's eyes, they will fall in love with anyone.

00:38:43.660 --> 00:38:45.150
Or anything.

00:38:45.210 --> 00:38:46.981
Find it for me, Puck.

00:38:47.041 --> 00:38:48.492
said Oberon.

00:38:48.552 --> 00:38:51.253
I'll bring you that flower immediately.

00:38:51.313 --> 00:38:55.555
Said Puck, I can fly around the world in 40 minutes.

00:38:55.615 --> 00:38:57.398
Puck flew off.

00:38:57.458 --> 00:38:59.842
Oberon waited for Puck.

00:38:59.902 --> 00:39:03.733
Then suddenly a young man ran past him.

00:39:03.793 --> 00:39:06.764
He couldn't see Oberon because of his magic.

00:39:06.824 --> 00:39:10.136
A pretty young woman with red hair followed the man.

00:39:10.196 --> 00:39:13.147
She looked sad and tired.

00:39:13.207 --> 00:39:17.078
The two young people were Demetrius and Helena.

00:39:17.138 --> 00:39:20.910
Demetrius was looking for Hermia and Lysander.

00:39:20.970 --> 00:39:22.871
He wanted to stop them.

00:39:22.931 --> 00:39:26.192
Helena only wanted to be with Demetrius.

00:39:26.252 --> 00:39:29.764
Don't follow me, Demetrius shouted.

00:39:29.824 --> 00:39:31.916
Go home, Helena.

00:39:31.976 --> 00:39:33.867
Please, Demetrius.

00:39:33.927 --> 00:39:35.158
said Helena.

00:39:35.218 --> 00:39:37.158
I want to come with you.

00:39:37.218 --> 00:39:39.920
Where are Lysander and Hermia?

00:39:39.980 --> 00:39:41.671
said Demetrius.

00:39:41.731 --> 00:39:45.763
I'll kill Lysander, and I'll bring Hermia back to Athens.

00:39:45.823 --> 00:39:48.264
She'll be my wife, not his.

00:39:48.324 --> 00:39:50.446
Where are they?

00:39:50.506 --> 00:39:52.616
I don't know.

00:39:52.676 --> 00:39:53.944
said Helena.

00:39:54.004 --> 00:39:56.833
I only know that they are in this wood.

00:39:56.893 --> 00:40:00.044
Please, I only want to be near you.

00:40:00.064 --> 00:40:03.246
I don't love you, said Demetrius.

00:40:03.306 --> 00:40:05.557
I don't even want to look at you.

00:40:05.617 --> 00:40:07.288
Helena began to cry.

00:40:07.308 --> 00:40:10.629
I love you Demetrius.

00:40:10.689 --> 00:40:16.101
She said Demetrius pushed Helena and she fell.

00:40:16.161 --> 00:40:19.462
Don't follow me, he said.

00:40:19.522 --> 00:40:22.558
Please don't come near me.

00:40:22.618 --> 00:40:24.282
He ran away.

00:40:24.342 --> 00:40:26.964
Helena slowly stood up.

00:40:27.024 --> 00:40:29.554
I need to be near him.

00:40:29.614 --> 00:40:31.035
She thought.

00:40:31.095 --> 00:40:34.016
She followed Demetrius into the wood.

00:40:34.076 --> 00:40:36.297
Oberon watched Helena.

00:40:36.357 --> 00:40:38.778
That poor sweet lady.

00:40:38.838 --> 00:40:40.878
He said to himself.

00:40:40.938 --> 00:40:43.029
He wanted to help her.

00:40:43.089 --> 00:40:45.210
Just then, Puck returned.

00:40:45.270 --> 00:40:47.400
He had the magic flower.

00:40:47.460 --> 00:40:49.301
Oberon smiled.

00:40:49.361 --> 00:40:51.775
Excellent, he said.

00:40:51.835 --> 00:40:54.799
Titania will go to sleep soon.

00:40:54.859 --> 00:40:59.232
I'll find her and put the juice of this flower on her eyes.

00:40:59.292 --> 00:41:05.034
She'll wake up and she'll fall in love with anything.

00:41:05.094 --> 00:41:09.397
Perhaps a bear or a bird or even a monkey.

00:41:09.457 --> 00:41:11.048
It doesn't matter.

00:41:11.108 --> 00:41:16.250
When she sees it, she will love it.

00:41:16.310 --> 00:41:18.752
He laughed.

00:41:18.812 --> 00:41:21.059
Then he remembered Helena.

00:41:21.119 --> 00:41:24.066
I saw a young man and a young woman here.

00:41:24.126 --> 00:41:25.638
He said to Puck.

00:41:25.698 --> 00:41:27.509
They're from Athens.

00:41:27.569 --> 00:41:30.491
The woman loves the man, but he hates her.

00:41:30.551 --> 00:41:33.513
Put the juice of this flower on the man's eyes.

00:41:33.573 --> 00:41:35.514
He'll fall in love with her.

00:41:35.574 --> 00:41:36.935
Can you do this?

00:41:36.995 --> 00:41:39.126
Of course, said Puck.

00:41:39.187 --> 00:41:40.337
It's easy.

00:41:40.398 --> 00:41:43.610
I'll look for the two young people from Athens.

00:41:43.670 --> 00:41:45.541
He flew away.

00:41:45.601 --> 00:41:48.948
Later, Oberon found Titania.

00:41:49.009 --> 00:41:52.235
She was sleeping on a bed of flowers near the river.

00:41:52.295 --> 00:41:56.326
Oberon put the juice of the flower onto Titania's eyes.

00:41:56.386 --> 00:41:59.837
Soon, you'll fall in love.

00:41:59.897 --> 00:42:08.604
He said to her, I hope that you will love something horrible.

00:42:08.664 --> 00:42:20.626
Countries all over the world have stories about fairies and some of these stories are very, very old.

00:42:20.686 --> 00:42:27.950
In these stories fairies looked like people, but they could fly and use magic.

00:42:28.011 --> 00:42:31.273
Sometimes they were bigger than people.

00:42:31.333 --> 00:42:36.622
Sometimes they were smaller and they had no wings.

00:42:36.682 --> 00:42:45.639
People believed that fairies could do good things and bad things, that they could sometimes hurt people or animals.

00:42:45.699 --> 00:42:51.570
They also believed that people lost their way in woods because of fairies.

00:42:51.630 --> 00:42:59.442
People even thought that fairies sometimes stole babies and children and kept them.

00:42:59.502 --> 00:43:08.290
In a Midsummer Night's Dream, Titania and Oberon have a child with them from India who is not a fairy.

00:43:08.350 --> 00:43:15.772
Sometimes people did strange things because they wanted to be safe from fairy magic.

00:43:15.832 --> 00:43:23.798
They often kept some cold iron in their houses because they thought that fairies were afraid of it.

00:43:23.858 --> 00:43:28.872
When they were in a wood, they sometimes carried bread with them.

00:43:28.932 --> 00:43:35.510
People with houses on a fairy road kept their doors open all night.

00:43:35.570 --> 00:43:41.226
Old stories all agree that only animals can see fairies.

00:43:41.286 --> 00:43:43.866
People usually can't see them.

00:43:43.926 --> 00:43:50.770
But if fairies want to appear, they can use their magic and people can see them.

00:43:50.830 --> 00:43:57.924
In a Midsummer Night's Dream, no one can see Oberon and Puck except other fairies.

00:43:57.984 --> 00:44:04.460
Later you will read that one person, Bottom, can see Titania and her fairies.

00:44:04.520 --> 00:44:08.786
This is because she wants to appear to him.

00:44:08.846 --> 00:44:14.320
Through the years, people's ideas about fairies slowly changed.

00:44:14.380 --> 00:44:20.996
In stories, fairies became smaller and prettier, and they usually had wings.

00:44:21.056 --> 00:44:24.529
They were good and never hurt people.

00:44:24.590 --> 00:44:28.102
This is our idea of fairies today.

00:44:28.162 --> 00:44:31.025
Do you believe in fairies?

00:44:31.085 --> 00:44:33.779
Be careful if you are in a wood.

00:44:33.839 --> 00:44:39.065
and take some bread and cold iron with you.

00:44:39.125 --> 00:44:50.724
Chapter 3 Puck's Mistake In another part of the wood, Lysander and Hermia were lost.

00:44:50.784 --> 00:44:56.360
They walked together for hours through the trees, but they couldn't find a way out of the wood.

00:44:56.420 --> 00:44:58.631
They both felt very tired.

00:44:58.691 --> 00:45:00.352
Their feet hurt.

00:45:00.412 --> 00:45:02.342
They wanted to sleep.

00:45:02.402 --> 00:45:04.632
they continued walking.

00:45:04.692 --> 00:45:09.512
Finally, they stopped at a quiet place near a river.

00:45:09.572 --> 00:45:12.743
Let's rest here, Hermia.

00:45:12.803 --> 00:45:14.313
said Lysander.

00:45:14.374 --> 00:45:16.924
We can start again tomorrow.

00:45:16.984 --> 00:45:19.225
That's a good idea.

00:45:19.285 --> 00:45:20.635
said Hermia.

00:45:20.695 --> 00:45:24.986
She lay down on the soft grass by the side of the river.

00:45:25.046 --> 00:45:27.166
Good night, Lysander.

00:45:27.226 --> 00:45:30.999
She said, and she fell asleep immediately.

00:45:31.059 --> 00:45:34.052
Lysander looked at her for a moment.

00:45:34.112 --> 00:45:36.922
I'll always love her.

00:45:36.982 --> 00:45:38.312
He thought.

00:45:38.373 --> 00:45:43.144
Soon he was asleep too, not far from Hermia.

00:45:43.204 --> 00:45:49.385
At the same time, Puck was flying through the trees with magic flower in his hand.

00:45:49.445 --> 00:45:56.386
He was looking for a young man and a young woman from Athens, but he couldn't see anyone.

00:45:56.446 --> 00:45:58.287
Where are they?

00:45:58.347 --> 00:45:59.397
He thought.

00:45:59.457 --> 00:46:02.429
Oberon will be angry if I don't find them.

00:46:02.489 --> 00:46:05.701
Then he saw Lysander and Hermia.

00:46:05.761 --> 00:46:07.632
At last?

00:46:07.692 --> 00:46:08.984
He said.

00:46:09.044 --> 00:46:12.206
A young man and young woman from Athens.

00:46:12.266 --> 00:46:15.487
He flew down and looked at Lysander.

00:46:15.548 --> 00:46:18.840
Now, what did Oberon say?

00:46:18.900 --> 00:46:20.552
He asked himself.

00:46:20.612 --> 00:46:25.645
She loves him, but he hates her.

00:46:25.705 --> 00:46:28.336
Well, that will change.

00:46:28.397 --> 00:46:32.808
He put the juice of the magic flower on Lysander's eyes.

00:46:32.868 --> 00:46:35.128
There, he said.

00:46:35.188 --> 00:46:40.239
He'll wake up, he'll see her, and he'll fall in love.

00:46:40.299 --> 00:46:42.290
He flew away.

00:46:42.350 --> 00:46:46.321
Demetrius was still looking for Hermia and Lysander.

00:46:46.381 --> 00:46:49.551
Poor Helena was still following Demetrius.

00:46:49.611 --> 00:46:58.134
Sometimes Demetrius ran too quickly, and sometimes he shouted at her, but she still followed him.

00:46:58.194 --> 00:47:03.756
They came to the place by the river, where Hermia and Lysander were sleeping.

00:47:03.816 --> 00:47:09.118
It was very dark, and so Demetrius and Helena didn't see them.

00:47:09.178 --> 00:47:12.279
Please wait for me, Demetrius!

00:47:12.339 --> 00:47:13.960
Helena said.

00:47:14.020 --> 00:47:19.032
For the last time, Helena, go home, Demetrius shouted.

00:47:19.092 --> 00:47:21.353
He ran away quickly.

00:47:21.413 --> 00:47:24.631
This time, Helena didn't follow him.

00:47:24.691 --> 00:47:26.609
She was too tired.

00:47:26.669 --> 00:47:29.911
She sat down on a rock and looked at the river.

00:47:29.971 --> 00:47:32.623
He's running away from me.

00:47:32.683 --> 00:47:33.854
She thought.

00:47:33.914 --> 00:47:35.955
And he's running to her.

00:47:36.015 --> 00:47:38.006
Lucky Hermia.

00:47:38.066 --> 00:47:40.268
Then she saw Lysander.

00:47:40.328 --> 00:47:42.379
He was sleeping on the grass.

00:47:42.439 --> 00:47:44.770
She was very surprised.

00:47:44.830 --> 00:47:48.263
Lysander, what are you doing here?

00:47:48.323 --> 00:47:49.824
Are you all right?

00:47:49.884 --> 00:47:51.225
She asked.

00:47:51.285 --> 00:47:54.292
Lysander opened his eyes slowly.

00:47:54.352 --> 00:47:58.678
The most beautiful woman in the world was looking at him.

00:47:58.738 --> 00:48:00.629
It was Helena.

00:48:00.689 --> 00:48:03.550
She's so lovely.

00:48:03.610 --> 00:48:06.761
She's wonderful, he thought.

00:48:06.821 --> 00:48:09.892
Why didn't I see it before?

00:48:09.952 --> 00:48:13.633
He remembered that Helena loved Demetrius.

00:48:13.693 --> 00:48:16.394
Suddenly he got very angry.

00:48:16.454 --> 00:48:18.545
Wake up, Lysander.

00:48:18.605 --> 00:48:20.325
said Helena.

00:48:20.385 --> 00:48:23.154
Lysander stood up quickly.

00:48:23.214 --> 00:48:25.492
Anything for you, Helena.

00:48:25.552 --> 00:48:27.392
Where is Demetrius?

00:48:27.452 --> 00:48:29.042
I'll kill him.

00:48:29.102 --> 00:48:35.724
Helena didn't understand Lysander's strange words or the strange look in his eyes.

00:48:35.784 --> 00:48:37.214
No, Lysander.

00:48:37.274 --> 00:48:39.485
Don't be angry with Demetrius.

00:48:39.545 --> 00:48:40.495
She said.

00:48:40.555 --> 00:48:45.036
I know he loves Hermia, but she only wants you.

00:48:45.096 --> 00:48:46.722
Hermia?

00:48:46.783 --> 00:48:48.349
said Lysander.

00:48:48.409 --> 00:48:50.810
I'm not interested in Hermia.

00:48:50.870 --> 00:48:53.882
I love you, not her.

00:48:53.942 --> 00:48:56.174
That's not funny, Lysander.

00:48:56.234 --> 00:48:57.955
Don't joke about that.

00:48:58.015 --> 00:48:59.196
said Helena.

00:48:59.256 --> 00:49:00.867
It's not a joke.

00:49:00.927 --> 00:49:02.688
I love you.

00:49:02.748 --> 00:49:04.720
said Lysander.

00:49:04.780 --> 00:49:07.492
Helena got very angry.

00:49:07.552 --> 00:49:09.383
This is too much.

00:49:09.443 --> 00:49:11.864
First Demetrius ran away from me.

00:49:11.924 --> 00:49:13.952
Now you're laughing at me.

00:49:14.012 --> 00:49:16.149
Helena turned and ran.

00:49:16.209 --> 00:49:17.390
No, wait!

00:49:17.450 --> 00:49:19.002
said Lysander.

00:49:19.062 --> 00:49:21.303
Then he remembered Hermia.

00:49:21.363 --> 00:49:23.774
She was still asleep on the grass.

00:49:23.834 --> 00:49:25.926
Lysander looked at her.

00:49:25.986 --> 00:49:29.509
Did I really love this girl?

00:49:29.569 --> 00:49:31.940
She's nothing.

00:49:32.000 --> 00:49:33.592
He thought.

00:49:33.652 --> 00:49:36.734
He followed Helena into the wood.

00:49:36.794 --> 00:49:41.456
Later, Hermia woke up with a scream.

00:49:41.516 --> 00:49:45.315
Lysander, I had a bad dream.

00:49:45.375 --> 00:49:46.565
She said.

00:49:46.626 --> 00:49:49.496
Lysander, where are you?

00:49:49.556 --> 00:49:52.158
Lysander didn't answer her.

00:49:52.218 --> 00:49:55.539
She couldn't see him or hear him anywhere.

00:49:55.599 --> 00:49:57.250
He was gone.

00:49:57.310 --> 00:49:59.971
She suddenly felt afraid.

00:50:00.031 --> 00:50:02.132
What happened to him?

00:50:02.192 --> 00:50:03.873
Is he in danger?

00:50:03.933 --> 00:50:05.584
Where is he?

00:50:05.644 --> 00:50:07.204
She thought.

00:50:07.264 --> 00:50:11.062
I have to find him.

00:50:11.122 --> 00:50:14.549
Chapter 4.

00:50:14.609 --> 00:50:16.590
The Actors.

00:50:16.650 --> 00:50:22.164
By the river on her bed of flowers, Queen Titania was sleeping.

00:50:22.225 --> 00:50:25.776
The juice of the magic flower was on her eyes.

00:50:25.837 --> 00:50:28.008
Puck watched her.

00:50:28.069 --> 00:50:32.371
Soon she'll wake up and she'll fall in love.

00:50:32.431 --> 00:50:38.936
He thought, will it be a bear or a dog or a bird?

00:50:38.996 --> 00:50:40.497
Well, it happens.

00:50:40.557 --> 00:50:42.795
I must tell Oberon.

00:50:42.856 --> 00:50:45.584
Suddenly he heard voices.

00:50:45.645 --> 00:50:51.288
A group of men from Athens were talking very close to the place where Titania was sleeping.

00:50:51.348 --> 00:50:54.180
Puck decided to listen to them.

00:50:54.240 --> 00:50:56.962
The men were practicing a play.

00:50:57.022 --> 00:51:02.116
They wanted to show this play at Theseus and Hippolyta's wedding.

00:51:02.176 --> 00:51:05.097
These men weren't really actors.

00:51:05.157 --> 00:51:07.538
This was just their hobby.

00:51:07.598 --> 00:51:10.140
They all had different jobs.

00:51:10.201 --> 00:51:12.508
One of the men was a tailor.

00:51:12.568 --> 00:51:14.444
One was a carpenter.

00:51:14.504 --> 00:51:15.955
One had a shop.

00:51:16.015 --> 00:51:18.486
Others built walls and houses.

00:51:18.546 --> 00:51:21.406
They were not the best actors in the world.

00:51:21.466 --> 00:51:24.488
In fact, they were very bad.

00:51:24.548 --> 00:51:29.669
But they loved acting and they always tried their best.

00:51:29.729 --> 00:51:34.610
One of the actors, Bottom, loved acting the most.

00:51:34.670 --> 00:51:40.882
He was a large kind man with a round face who always smiled.

00:51:40.942 --> 00:51:42.744
Bottom?

00:51:42.804 --> 00:51:45.506
You will be the hero of this play.

00:51:45.567 --> 00:51:47.998
said his friend Peter Quince.

00:51:48.058 --> 00:51:51.832
There is also a lady and a lion.

00:51:51.892 --> 00:51:54.313
I can be all of them.

00:51:54.374 --> 00:51:55.694
said Bottom.

00:51:55.754 --> 00:52:03.228
I'll be a handsome hero and a pretty lady and a dangerous lion.

00:52:03.288 --> 00:52:05.650
Theseus will love it.

00:52:05.710 --> 00:52:07.771
You'll be the hero, Bottom.

00:52:07.831 --> 00:52:09.192
Said Peter.

00:52:09.252 --> 00:52:11.234
Only the hero.

00:52:11.294 --> 00:52:14.546
Now, go behind that tree and practice.

00:52:14.607 --> 00:52:17.218
I'll call you when we need you.

00:52:17.278 --> 00:52:20.341
Bottom went behind a large tree.

00:52:20.401 --> 00:52:22.232
Puck was watching.

00:52:22.292 --> 00:52:24.734
Is this the hero?

00:52:24.794 --> 00:52:26.056
He thought.

00:52:26.116 --> 00:52:28.557
He laughed.

00:52:28.617 --> 00:52:32.636
I have a wonderful idea.

00:52:32.696 --> 00:52:35.313
Puck used his magic.

00:52:35.374 --> 00:52:38.755
Bottom suddenly felt very strange.

00:52:38.816 --> 00:52:40.846
His ears began to grow.

00:52:40.906 --> 00:52:43.288
His nose got bigger and bigger.

00:52:43.348 --> 00:52:45.159
His teeth got larger.

00:52:45.219 --> 00:52:49.431
And hair began to grow all over his face.

00:52:49.492 --> 00:52:52.164
What's happening?

00:52:52.224 --> 00:52:56.706
He said, and his voice was very strange.

00:52:56.766 --> 00:53:01.339
Soon, poor Bottom had a large ugly donkey's head.

00:53:01.399 --> 00:53:03.530
Puck smiled.

00:53:03.590 --> 00:53:06.042
Where's the hero?

00:53:06.102 --> 00:53:08.242
Called Peter Quince.

00:53:08.303 --> 00:53:09.704
Bottom?

00:53:09.764 --> 00:53:11.325
We need you.

00:53:11.385 --> 00:53:14.648
Bottom came out from behind the tree.

00:53:14.708 --> 00:53:16.528
Here I am.

00:53:16.589 --> 00:53:19.290
He said in his strange voice.

00:53:19.350 --> 00:53:21.582
I'm the hero.

00:53:21.642 --> 00:53:23.704
Where's my lady?

00:53:23.764 --> 00:53:26.636
His friends screamed.

00:53:26.696 --> 00:53:28.968
He's a monster!

00:53:29.028 --> 00:53:30.238
They said.

00:53:30.299 --> 00:53:32.580
They ran away quickly.

00:53:32.640 --> 00:53:39.274
Bottom, look at yourself, said Peter Quince, and then he followed the others.

00:53:39.335 --> 00:53:42.516
Bottom couldn't see himself.

00:53:42.576 --> 00:53:45.868
Why are they running?

00:53:45.928 --> 00:53:47.950
He thought.

00:53:48.010 --> 00:53:51.121
Are they playing a joke?

00:53:51.182 --> 00:53:54.420
I know that you're joking.

00:53:54.480 --> 00:53:57.487
I'm not afraid.

00:53:57.547 --> 00:53:58.918
Do you hear me?

00:53:58.978 --> 00:54:00.819
I feel fine.

00:54:00.879 --> 00:54:02.340
I'll sing.

00:54:02.400 --> 00:54:03.951
I'll sing.

00:54:04.011 --> 00:54:04.882
I'll sing.

00:54:04.942 --> 00:54:05.512
I'll sing.

00:54:05.572 --> 00:54:06.012
I'll sing.

00:54:06.032 --> 00:54:06.323
I'll sing.

00:54:06.383 --> 00:54:07.033
I'll sing.

00:54:07.093 --> 00:54:08.564
I'll sing.

00:54:08.624 --> 00:54:09.895
I'll sing.

00:54:09.955 --> 00:54:10.615
I'll sing.

00:54:10.675 --> 00:54:11.736
I'll sing.

00:54:11.756 --> 00:54:12.937
I'll sing.

00:54:12.997 --> 00:54:18.282
I'll sing.

00:54:18.342 --> 00:54:26.638
Soon he came to the place where Titania was asleep.

00:54:26.698 --> 00:54:28.879
Her eyes opened.

00:54:28.939 --> 00:54:31.060
That song?

00:54:31.120 --> 00:54:32.561
She thought.

00:54:32.621 --> 00:54:34.251
That voice.

00:54:34.311 --> 00:54:36.682
It's beautiful.

00:54:36.742 --> 00:54:38.903
Then she saw a Bottom.

00:54:38.963 --> 00:54:45.126
She looked at Bottom ugly long ears and his long nose and his big teeth.

00:54:45.186 --> 00:54:49.517
She thought that he was the most beautiful person in the world.

00:54:49.577 --> 00:54:52.143
Titania stood up quickly.

00:54:52.203 --> 00:54:56.340
She said, please sing again.

00:54:56.400 --> 00:55:01.043
Your song is so lovely, and you are so handsome.

00:55:01.103 --> 00:55:03.965
I don't know you, but I love you."

00:55:04.025 --> 00:55:07.156
Bottom was very surprised.

00:55:07.216 --> 00:55:09.188
We?

00:55:09.248 --> 00:55:12.550
Do you think I'm handsome?

00:55:12.610 --> 00:55:14.791
Do you love me?

00:55:14.851 --> 00:55:16.092
He said.

00:55:16.152 --> 00:55:19.993
He smiled and showed his big yellow teeth.

00:55:20.053 --> 00:55:25.174
Oh, this is a dream, he thought.

00:55:25.234 --> 00:55:29.036
And it's a very good dream.

00:55:29.096 --> 00:55:32.267
Yes, of course I love you.

00:55:32.327 --> 00:55:33.767
Titania said.

00:55:33.827 --> 00:55:36.888
Please, stay here in the wood with me.

00:55:36.908 --> 00:55:39.560
I am the queen of the fairies.

00:55:39.620 --> 00:55:42.670
My servants will bring you anything.

00:55:42.730 --> 00:55:46.017
Titania called her fairy servants.

00:55:46.077 --> 00:55:49.044
Suddenly there were fairies everywhere.

00:55:49.104 --> 00:55:52.086
They flew and danced around Titania.

00:55:52.146 --> 00:55:54.857
This is my love.

00:55:54.917 --> 00:55:59.150
She said to them, bring him food and flowers.

00:55:59.210 --> 00:56:01.922
Bottom couldn't believe his luck.

00:56:01.982 --> 00:56:06.904
He walked through the wood hand in hand with beautiful Titania.

00:56:06.964 --> 00:56:09.526
Puck laughed and laughed.

00:56:09.586 --> 00:56:11.428
He flew through the trees.

00:56:11.488 --> 00:56:15.798
Then he found Oberon, and he told him the whole story.

00:56:15.859 --> 00:56:18.008
This is wonderful.

00:56:18.068 --> 00:56:19.670
said Oberon.

00:56:19.730 --> 00:56:24.364
He laughed.

00:56:24.424 --> 00:56:31.340
The queen of the fairies is in love with an ugly monster.

00:56:31.400 --> 00:56:32.692
Good work, Puck.